# Terraform tfvars stay with the user

`terraform.tfvars` holds live secrets and is gitignored. Do not read, grep, diff, format, or quote it. The same applies to `*.auto.tfvars` and `*.tfvars.json`.

Stop at `terraform.tfvars.example`. When a variable is added or changed, update that template and tell the user what to set locally.

```bash
# ❌ BAD — fmt walks terraform.tfvars and prints its values
terraform fmt -check -diff

# ✅ GOOD — templates only
terraform fmt main.tf variables.tf terraform.tfvars.example
```

Do not run `terraform plan` or `terraform apply`. Those load the real tfvars. Leave apply and any check of live values to the user.
